Q: What product is the main driver for adding pagination to searchEmployer?
A: The pagination enhancement for **searchEmployer** was driven by **Royal London** — the wiki page is hosted in the client-specific "CliRln" (Client Royal London) space, and the originating requirement is titled "RLSI-6059 searchEmployer SBS to support pagination," an RLSI-prefixed (Royal London Solution/Initiative) ticket linked to components **SBS/Workplace** (Jira: RLSI-6059 — searchEmployer SBS to support pagination; Wiki: RLSI-6059 searchEmployer SBS to support pagination § Solution Overview).

The associated work package FEAT-9707 confirms the same origin (Jira: FEAT-9707 — RLSI-6059 - searchEmployer SBS to support pagination and return employer external refs), and the underlying rationale — supporting higher Employer volumes with consistent ordering, total-count visibility, and incremental retrieval — reflects Royal London's scale/performance needs for their Workplace pension scheme employer base (Jira: BASE-458911 — Sonata Business Services (SBS) - Operation searchEmployer added with optional element pagingRange... to support pagination for higher Employer volumes, ensuring search flexibility).
